<title>UK: Nigeria tells OPEC it pumped 1.89 mbpd in December.</title>
<headline>Nigeria tells OPEC it pumped 1.89 mbpd in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria told OPEC it produced 1.89 million barrels per day (bpd) in December, the OPEC News Agency OPECNA said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Nigeria has an OPEC quota of 1.865 million bpd.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of officials, industry monitors and analysts put the country's December wellhead output at 2.06 million bpd, 10,000 bpd above the November estimate.</p>
<p>OPEC sets its quotas according to supply to the market and not by wellhead output. Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>December production and supply data received so far by the OPEC Secretariat is as follows (in 1,000 bpd):</p>
<p>COUNTRY	  PRODUCTION	SUPPLY     QUOTA</p>
<p>-------	  ----------	------     -----</p>
<p>ALGERIA	   793.0	     760.0	750.0</p>
<p>INDONESIA     1,326.9	   1,326.6    1,330.0</p>
<p>IRAN	    3,594.0	   3,594.0    3,600.0</p>
<p>KUWAIT	  2,003.1	   2,004.8    2,000.0</p>
<p>LIBYA	   1,398.0	   1,397.0    1,390.0</p>
<p>NIGERIA	 1,889.6	   1,865.0    1,865.0</p>
<p>QATAR	     394.1	     381.7	378.0</p>
<p>SAUDI ARABIA  8,008.1	   7,989.3    8,000.0</p>
<p>UAE	     2,162.2	   2,180.0    2,161.0</p>
<p>VENEZUELA     2,391.0	   2,381.0    2,359.0</p>
